<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Arabia and the Gulf</p><h1 class="st-title">Ayyubid Yemen</h1><p class="st-meta">1174 CE – 1229 CE · capital Ta'izz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Yemen as a dominion of Saladin's family, which ended its many local dynasties and made Ta'izz a royal centre.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1174 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> sent his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turan-shah-ibn-ayyub">Turan-Shah</a> with an army to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Yemen</a>. He defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/mahdid-dynasty">Mahdid dynasty</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zabid">Zabid</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/zurayid-dynasty">Zurayid dynasty</a> and pressed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/hamdanid-sultanate-of-yemen">Hamdanid sultanate of Yemen</a>, uniting the lowlands and much of the south under the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-yemen">Yemen</a> was ruled by Ayyubid princes as a valuable dependency, profiting from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden's</a> customs and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-sea">Red Sea</a> trade. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tughtakin-ibn-ayyub">Tughtakin ibn Ayyub</a>, ruler from 1182 to 1197, consolidated control, took Sanaa and made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiz">Ta'izz</a> an important base. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubids</a> promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunni-islam">Sunni Islam</a>, founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasas</a> and introduced Kurdish and Turkic troops. The Zaydi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imams</a> resisted in the northern highlands.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1229 the last Ayyubid ruler, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-masud-yusuf">al-Mas'ud Yusuf</a>, left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, appointing his commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din-umar-ibn-rasul">Nur al-Din Umar ibn Rasul</a> as deputy. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nur-al-din">Nur al-Din</a> soon declared independence, founding the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/rasulid-dynasty">Rasulid dynasty</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="other, 1174 CE – 1229 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M26 24 H74 V52 Q74 74 50 84 Q26 74 26 52 Z"/><path d="M50 24 V84 M26 46 H74"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">other</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Arabia and the Gulf</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:83.06%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1174 CE – 1229 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ta'izz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Turan-Shah, Tughtakin ibn Ayyub, al-Mas'ud Yusuf</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/yemen">Yemen</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Ayyubid Sultanate of Yemen</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1202&amp;focus=ayyubid-yemen" aria-label="Ayyubid Yemen on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5886 1672 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Ayyubid Yemen lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6206 1928L5811 1337M6206 1928L6206 1928"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5811 1337h0M6206 1928h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6206 1928h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6206 1928h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Ta'izz. <a href="/atlas?year=1202&amp;focus=ayyubid-yemen">On the atlas &